{"slug":"/students/subjects/english/core-grammar/","source":"students/subjects/english/core-grammar/index.html","area":"students","kind":"division","title":"Core Grammar — English","description":"","subject":"english","body":"<div class=\"max-w-5xl mx-auto\">\n    <nav class=\"mb-6\"><a href=\"/students/subjects/english/\" class=\"text-blue-600\">← Back to English</a></nav>\n    <header class=\"mb-4\">\n      <h1 class=\"text-3xl font-bold\">Core Grammar in Use</h1>\n      <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Apply sentence building blocks: tense, concord, verbals, sentence types and reported forms.</p>\n    </header>\n\n    <section class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4\">\n      <div class=\"card p-5 rounded-lg\"><h3 class=\"font-semibold\"><a href=\"/students/subjects/english/core-grammar/tense-aspect/\" class=\"hover:text-blue-600\">Tense &amp; Aspect</a></h3><p class=\"text-sm text-gray-700\">Simple, continuous and perfect usages across time frames.</p></div>\n      <div class=\"card p-5 rounded-lg\"><h3 class=\"font-semibold\"><a href=\"/students/subjects/english/core-grammar/concord-verbals/\" class=\"hover:text-blue-600\">Concord &amp; Verbals</a></h3><p class=\"text-sm text-gray-700\">Subject-verb agreement and infinitives, gerunds &amp; participles.</p></div>\n      <div class=\"card p-5 rounded-lg\"><h3 class=\"font-semibold\"><a href=\"/students/subjects/english/core-grammar/infinitives-gerunds-participles/\" class=\"hover:text-blue-600\">Infinitives, Gerunds &amp; Participles</a></h3><p class=\"text-sm text-gray-700\">Functions and common exam patterns.</p></div>\n      <div class=\"card p-5 rounded-lg\"><h3 class=\"font-semibold\"><a href=\"/students/subjects/english/core-grammar/sentence-classification/\" class=\"hover:text-blue-600\">Sentence Classification</a></h3><p class=\"text-sm text-gray-700\">Simple, compound, complex and compound-complex structures.</p></div>\n      <div class=\"card p-5 rounded-lg\"><h3 class=\"font-semibold\"><a href=\"/students/subjects/english/core-grammar/reported-speech-question-tags/\" class=\"hover:text-blue-600\">Reported Speech &amp; Question Tags</a></h3><p class=\"text-sm text-gray-700\">Shifts in tense, reporting verbs and tag question formation.</p></div>\n      <div class=\"card p-5 rounded-lg\"><h3 class=\"font-semibold\"><a href=\"/students/subjects/english/core-grammar/phrasal-verbs-idioms/\" class=\"hover:text-blue-600\">Phrasal Verbs &amp; Idioms</a></h3><p class=\"text-sm text-gray-700\">High-frequency phrasal verbs and idiomatic expressions.</p></div>\n      <div class=\"card p-5 rounded-lg\"><h3 class=\"font-semibold\"><a href=\"/students/subjects/english/core-grammar/antonyms-synonyms-homonyms/\" class=\"hover:text-blue-600\">Antonyms, Synonyms &amp; Homonyms</a></h3><p class=\"text-sm text-gray-700\">Precision in word choice and common pitfalls.</p></div>\n      <div class=\"card p-5 rounded-lg\"><h3 class=\"font-semibold\"><a href=\"/students/subjects/english/core-grammar/language-registers/\" class=\"hover:text-blue-600\">Language Registers</a></h3><p class=\"text-sm text-gray-700\">Formal, informal and academic registers with examples.</p></div>\n    </section>\n  </div>\n\n\n\n\n\n  <meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n  <title>Core Grammar | English</title>\n  \n  <link href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;600&amp;display=swap\" rel=\"stylesheet\">\n  <style> body{font-family:Inter, sans-serif}.card{-webkit-backdrop-filter:blur(14px);backdrop-filter:blur(14px);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.3);}</style>\n\n\n  <div class=\"max-w-4xl mx-auto\">\n    <nav class=\"mb-6\"><a href=\"/students/subjects/english/\" class=\"text-blue-600\">← Back to English</a></nav>\n    <h1 class=\"text-3xl font-bold mb-4\">Core Grammar in Use</h1>\n    <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-6\">Tenses, concord, verbals, sentence classification and reported speech.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n      <article class=\"card p-5 rounded-lg\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold\"><a href=\"/students/subjects/english/core-grammar/\" class=\"hover:text-blue-600\">Tenses &amp; Aspect</a></h2>\n        <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-700\">Practical use of simple, continuous, perfect and perfect-continuous tenses.</p>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card p-5 rounded-lg\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold\"><a href=\"/students/subjects/english/core-grammar/\" class=\"hover:text-blue-600\">Reported Speech</a></h2>\n        <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-700\">Converting direct speech to reported speech with backshift of tenses.</p>\n      </article>\n    </div>\n  </div>","bodyClass":"min-h-screen bg-gradient-to-br from-yellow-50 to-orange-100 p-6","bodyStyle":"","css":["body{font-family:Inter, sans-serif}.card{ -webkit-backdrop-filter:blur(14px);backdrop-filter:blur(14px);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.82);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18);box-shadow:0 6px 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.05);}","body{font-family:Inter, sans-serif}.card{-webkit-backdrop-filter:blur(14px);backdrop-filter:blur(14px);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.3);}"],"quiz":null,"tracker":null,"links":[]}